   106	| PACKAUTH-PRESERVE-TAUTOLOGY-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Stop preserve mode from making ordinal-1 PACK_AUTHENTICATION a tautology — the echo path re-emits the committed frozen bytes instead of re-deriving them, so `--check` compares those bytes with themselves | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Landed on PR #214 (branch `fix/packauth-soundness-rows`; gauntlet: design consult → implement → independent audit → fix round → delta re-audit → magistrate-authorized fix round 2 → second fresh delta re-audit). WHAT WAS WRONG, executed: with `PRESERVE_CURRENT_FROZEN_BYTES` true the generator's `_generate` writes every output straight from `REPO_ROOT` and RETURNS EARLY — even the pinned external-input drift checks are never reached — so a committed science-row tamper AND an acceptance-JSON drift each pass a preserve-mode `--check` with rc=0 (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/what-check-proves.md`, replayable via `replay-mutations.sh`). CURE, at two boundaries, with no frozen byte and no schema touched. (1) At the evidence author: every generator invocation is classified `regenerated` or `echo`, the preserve selection is EXPLICIT rather than inherited from the generator's compiled-in default, and an `echo` result can no longer produce `pack_generator_check_status: PASS`. (2) At the histsem verifier: an authenticated PACK_AUTHENTICATION item is re-derived at the coordinate its OWN source and receipt already record — source/receipt `head_commit` and `pack_sha256` must agree, that exact local-Git coordinate is materialized in a temporary checkout, and the plan-pinned generator runs there under explicit no-preserve, composed with the existing K5/K12/binding/closed-delta checks. A U11-PROJECTED coordinate uses the composed anchor+replay derivation instead of a bare check: a bare check at a projected coordinate refuses, because the projection rewrites `plan_tree.json`, `plan_tree.sha256` and `producer_contract.json` through a different serializer, and tre