    78	make the voided energy values usable.
    79	
    80	Unless a figure explicitly states otherwise, JouleWise uses gross measured
    81	energy within the named measurement boundary as the headline basis. Gross
    82	energy retains the idle, model-residency, and runtime overhead present during
    83	the measured interval, so comparisons across devices, configurations, and
    84	split versus monolithic execution use gross energy. Idle-subtracted energy is
    85	reported separately as a within-device secondary view of activity above the
    86	measured idle baseline; it is not used to rank devices or configurations. In
    87	Q4, the fixed term is estimated from the gross-energy workload sweep and is
    88	not set equal to measured idle energy. The advisor-review rationale and full
    89	basis/boundary rule are recorded in
