   119	## Attribution Limits
   120	
   121	The rows whose historical wording most invited over-attribution are:
   122	
   123	- `C5-1.1`: active-parameter energy scaling. The C-014 amendment caps
   124	  4-6-model designs at descriptive L2 pairwise contrasts unless the model set
   125	  grows enough for a predeclared one-covariate fit, and forbids fitting
   126	  active+total+KV covariates on 4-6 model points. The claims ladder also
   127	  prevents L1 active-parameter-scaling language; the capability map records
   128	  the current two-model observation as a non-claim.
   129	- `C5-1.8`: runtime energy attribution. The bank already says comparisons
   130	  where formats force different artifacts are stack-vs-stack comparisons.
   131	  The registry therefore forbids wording that energy "belongs to the runtime"
   132	  unless the artifact/runtime identity problem is actually controlled.
   133	
   134	This subsection is hygiene for claims indexing. It does not re-adjudicate the
   135	ratified C-014/C-015 bank decisions.

