78:where the one shared sign \(s\in\{-1,+1\}\) is the same for every block and each local sign \(e_j\in\{-1,+1\}\) is chosen independently. The replay enumerates both shared signs and every combination of local signs. At every such corner it recalculates the complete comparative unguarded floor—both the largest absolute block difference and the prediction expression built from the new mean and sample standard deviation—and retains the maximum. Dividing that maximum by the comparative point-only unguarded floor gives \(R_{cm}\). A comparative \(R_{cm}<2\) withdraws the boundary-dominance sentence even when independent-edge \(R\ge2\).
