   180	### Cell-label terms and D-165 attribution-dominance ratios
   181	
   182	D-165 reversed ruling item 34. TERM A and TERM B remain reproducible because
   183	the coded predicate survives as the cell label, but `TERM B > TERM A` is not
   184	the paper's headline falsifier. For component \(j\), the retained label terms
   185	are:
   186	
   187	```text
   188	A_unguarded_abs = max(max_abs_residual_j, prediction_component_j)
   189	A_guarded_abs   = guard_factor * A_unguarded_abs
   190	
   191	A_unguarded_cmp = max(max_abs_delta_j, prediction_component_j)
   192	A_guarded_cmp   = guard_factor * A_unguarded_cmp
   193	```
   194	
   195	TERM B is the exact linear corner maximum used by that same component's code
   196	predicate. Preserve the emitted array order and use `math.fsum` for \(W\):
   197	
   198	```text
   199	absolute:    n = cells[].absolute.n
   200	             r_i = cells[].absolute.residuals_j[i]
   201	             w_i = cells[].absolute.admissible_half_widths_j[i]
   202	             W = math.fsum(w_i)
   203	             B_abs = max_i(abs(r_i) + w_i*(n-1)/n + (W-w_i)/n)
   204	
   205	comparative: d_i = cells[].comparative.block_deltas_j[i]
   206	             w_i = cells[].comparative.admissible_half_widths_j[i]
   207	             B_cmp = max_i(abs(d_i) + w_i)
   208	```
   209	
   210	The headline ratio is instead
   211	`R = corner_widened_unguarded_floor_j / point_unguarded_floor_j`, evaluated
   212	separately for the absolute and comparative component of every cell. The point
   213	denominator is re-derived from unconditional parents as
   214	`max(max_abs_residual_j, prediction_component_j)` for absolute or
   215	`max(max_abs_delta_j, prediction_component_j)` for comparative. The numerator
   216	is the complete emitted `corner_widened_unguarded_floor_j`, not TERM B and not
   217	the guarded or drift-widened published floor. The gate is `R >= 2.0`; exact
   218	equality passes. A zero denominator refuses with
   219	`dominance_ratio_zero_denominator`. Every registered component in every cell
   220	must pass; mixed outcomes are printed per component and use null framing.
   221	
   222	Comparative R_cm is mandatory per cell. Its supplier is the registered
   223	`d165_shared_sign_local_corner_replay.v1` rule over authenticated custodied
   224	block inputs, before the producer's shared-plus-local composition destroys the
   225	split. `R_cm < 2.0` withdraws the dominance sentence even if independent-corner
   226	R passed. Absolute R_cm is not a missing value: it is registered
   227	`not_applicable` because the deviations-from-mean absolute estimator cancels a
   228	uniform shared fiducial shift exactly and the replay is comparative-only.
