    85	The interquartile range is the width of the middle half of the sample: a quarter
    86	of the values sit below it and a quarter above. The median absolute deviation is
    87	the typical distance of a value from the median, and is used here because it is
    88	not moved by the one or two extreme pulses.
    89	
    90	Worst excursions of the allowed intervals — the quantity the bound is built from,
    91	always positive because it is a distance from zero:
    92	
    93	| | Onsets (59) | Offsets (59) | All 118 |
    94	|---|---|---|---|
    95	| median | 14.924429 | 8.241330 | 11.903439 |
    96	| interquartile range | 5.126558 | 6.546343 | 7.599034 |
